Open each iconv file operand, not the first one every time.
The loop over the operands tested argv[i] for "-" but opened
argv[optind], so every file after the first converted the first file
again: iconv a b printed a twice. When the first operand was "-", each
later operand instead opened a file named "-", so iconv - a read stdin
and then failed with "can't open '-'". Open the operand the loop is on.

The loop also closed stdin after a "-" operand, so a second "-" read
from a closed stream. Leave stdin open, as cut, fold and grep do.

---
 miscutils/iconv.c |    4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/miscutils/iconv.c
+++ b/miscutils/iconv.c
@@ -1755,9 +1755,9 @@
 		if (argv[i][0] == '-' && argv[i][1] == '\0')
 			in = stdin;
 		else
-			in = xfopen(argv[optind], "rb");
+			in = xfopen(argv[i], "rb");
 		process_file(cd, in, out);
-		fclose(in);
+		fclose_if_not_stdin(in);
 	}
 
 	if (tmpname) {
